      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city was officially organized in 1854, but it didn’t get a courthouse until 1868.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Sterling%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Brown County was created from Schuyler County in 1839 and named after General Jacob Brown, who defeated the British at Sackett’s Harbor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.browncoil.org/about/history/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sterling was originally platted in 1833 by Alexander Curry, who also donated the land that became the town’s public square.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
